{"ts": 1791259945.5940669, "type": "step", "step": 20, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/environments.md", "section": "What an environment is"}, "output": "# Agent environments\n\n## What an environment is\nState, observations, actions, dynamics. The reward is a separate claim about what matters.\n\n## Partial observability (POMDP)\nWhen the agent cannot see the full state it must maintain a belief and sometimes act to gather information. Measurement can be an action with a cost.\n\n## Attention as a hidden variable\nLearners do not read everything shown to them. Attention gates learning and drains with fatigue.\n", "t": 1, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.20282525443759936, "pomdp": 0.20282525443759936, "pass_k": 0.20282525443759936}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7843091835012588, "motivation": 0.8589364796632395, "reliance": 0.45602770298460465, "persistence": 0.37480768876559933, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3439719309903426, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2920196205727638, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791259949.2192798, "type": "step", "step": 21, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Yep \u2014 the eval part is basically about reliability, not just whether it worked once. For your build, write something like: (1) what counts as success for one run, (2) which 3 seeds you used, and (3) report pass^3, meaning the build only 'passes' if all 3 seeded runs succeed. Also connect it to the reading: pass@k = at least one success, but pass^k = reliability across runs, which is stricter and better for deployment. After that, add 1\u20132 sentences on why this is a more direct measure than a vague proxy metric.\n\nCan you reply with your one-run success criterion in one sentence? I\u2019ll help tighten it.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3_eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\nStudent: can you just tell me the answer for pass^k?\n[activity] t=1 messages 2m", "t": 3, "activity": [{"t": 1, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.20282525443759936, "pomdp": 0.20282525443759936, "pass_k": 0.322408206230533}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7843091835012588, "motivation": 0.8589364796632395, "reliance": 0.4760277029846047, "persistence": 0.37480768876559933, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3439719309903426, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2920196205727638, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791259952.4916859, "type": "step", "step": 22, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I can\u2019t write the submission for you, but here\u2019s the key idea: pass^k means the agent counts as successful only if it succeeds on every one of k runs. So if you evaluate on 3 seeds, pass^3 = 1 only when all 3 runs succeed; otherwise pass^3 = 0. \n\nFor your writeup, use a fill-in template:\n- One-run success criterion: \u201cA run succeeds if ____.\u201d\n- Seeds used: s1, s2, s3\n- Result: \u201cWe report pass^3, which is 1 iff all three seeded runs satisfy the success criterion.\u201d\n- Why this metric: \u201cUnlike pass@k, which only needs one successful run, pass^k measures reliability across runs.\u201d\n\nReply with your actual success criterion and I\u2019ll help you polish it into final wording.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3_eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\n[activity] t=3 messages 2m", "t": 5, "activity": [{"t": 3, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.20282525443759936, "pomdp": 0.20282525443759936, "pass_k": 0.4470207539050357}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7843091835012588, "motivation": 0.8589364796632395, "reliance": 0.4960277029846047, "persistence": 0.37480768876559933, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3439719309903426, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2920196205727638, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791259954.680562, "type": "step", "step": 23, "action": "notes_append", "args": {"note_id": "writeup", "text": "\n\n## Evaluation scaffold\n- Define one-run success clearly.\n- Report results on at least 3 seeds.\n- Explain that pass^k means success only if all k runs succeed.\n- Contrast with pass@k, which only requires at least one success.\n- Add 1 sentence on why pass^k captures reliability better for deployment."}, "output": "Appended.", "t": 5, "activity": [], "events": [{"type": "note_edit", "note_id": "writeup", "by": "agent"}], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.20282525443759936, "pomdp": 0.20282525443759936, "pass_k": 0.4470207539050357}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7843091835012588, "motivation": 0.8589364796632395, "reliance": 0.4960277029846047, "persistence": 0.37480768876559933, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3439719309903426, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2920196205727638, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791259957.752288, "type": "step", "step": 24, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Quick version: pass^k is the strict reliability metric. If you use k=3 seeds, then pass^3 = 1 only if the agent succeeds on seed 1, seed 2, and seed 3; if any one fails, pass^3 = 0.\n\nUse that idea to finish your eval section. Try writing these two sentences in your own words:\n1) \u201cA single run is successful if ____.\u201d\n2) \u201cWe report pass^3 over three seeds, so the system only passes when all three runs succeed.\u201d\n\nIf you paste your sentence for (1), I\u2019ll help tighten it fast.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3_eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: nice, I think I see it now\nStudent: honestly can you just give me the answer, I'm stuck on pass^k\n[activity] t=5 messages 4m", "t": 9, "activity": [{"t": 5, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.20282525443759936, "pomdp": 0.20282525443759936, "pass_k": 0.5314291260055053}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7843091835012588, "motivation": 0.8589364796632395, "reliance": 0.4960277029846047, "persistence": 0.37480768876559933, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3439719309903426, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2920196205727638, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
